  "notes": "National Agricultural Development Co. (NADEC) — Saudi-Tadawul listed integrated dairy + agriculture group. Calendar fiscal year (Dec 31). Reportable IFRS 8 segments: Dairy + Foods (milk, juices, cheese, processed foods) and Agriculture (potato, vegetables, fruits, juice concentrate, olive oil — also includes large-scale arable farms in Saudi Arabia). NADEC owns ~50,000 ha (~124k acres) of farmland in Saudi Arabia (Haradh, Al-Jouf, Hail) including potato, alfalfa (legacy — winding down due to Saudi water restrictions on green-fodder cultivation), olives, table grapes. Most revenue (~75-80%) is dairy/foods; Agriculture is ~20-25%. Quarterly figures from Tadawul Form 8 quarterly disclosures and NADEC IR press releases; annual data from 2020-2024 annual reports. Net debt = total borrowings − cash & cash equivalents. Property book = property, plant & equipment + biological assets + bearer plants. Some segment splits estimated from disclosed annual breakdowns where quarterly disclosures are aggregate.",
